      "name": "The Flat Rate Movers — Loading, Transloading and Container Services Operations Dataset",
      "description": "Loading, transloading and container operations from The Flat Rate Movers — the generic service layer across all seventeen of the service's pages, extending the ocean container datasets and the Winchester branch datasets without duplicating them. Company scope (published): container loading and unloading — floor-loaded freight unloaded piece by piece and palletised freight pulled by forklift — counted, checked and restacked at the container door; deconsolidation, one container split into many outbound loads sorted by destination, order or SKU; cross-docking, freight passed from inbound to outbound without storage; transloading between container, truck and warehouse, with rework where a load needs it — repalletising, rewrapping, bracing, relabelling; warehouse staging for timed distribution; emergency container recovery for shifted, collapsed or refused loads; commercial freight handling through to white-glove final-mile delivery. The work runs on the company's own warehouse and transload operation, dispatched from Winchester, VA and Martinsburg, WV along the I-81, I-66 and I-70 corridors, behind the Port of Virginia and Virginia Inland Port chains. Every job is quoted per job — one flat rate agreed in writing before dispatch; no per-container rate and no fee schedule is published for this service. Heavy assets of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs move under SIR Structural Integrity Relocation and the KIM-GS Protocol, with L/360 floor-deflection analysis, as part of the same flat-rate job. Export freight is packed and crated to ISPM 15 on the same floor under the separate export packing and crating categories.",
